1. HIP kernel: bf16 A -> A_q [M, K//2] fp4x2 + A_scale [M, K//32] e8m0 LINEAR
2. B_scale unshuffle: B_scale_sh -> B_scale [N, K//32] (cheap reshape, ~0.1µs)
3. Triton tl.dot_scaled GEMM: A_q (row-major) x B_q (loaded transposed) -> C

Layout summary (gfx950 hardware requirements from Helion analysis):
- LHS:       a_tile  [BLOCK_M, BLOCK_K]    fp4x2 row-major
- LHS scale: a_scale [BLOCK_M, SCALE_PER_K] e8m0 row-major
- RHS:       b_tile  [BLOCK_K, BLOCK_N]    fp4x2 (loaded transposed from [N, K//2])
- RHS scale: b_scale [BLOCK_N, SCALE_PER_K] e8m0 N-first (gfx950 hardware constraint)
- BLOCK_K min = 64 packed fp4x2 bytes; SCALE_PER_K = BLOCK_K // 16
